From 7da88d973f9dc3f7c0153f7b5000ef8e7bba2e9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:57:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netproxy: the read after failed ones of the system's proxy is
 put off longer each time (#4169)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A read of the system's proxy is a fork() of scutil, and fork() in a
multithreaded process runs libmalloc's atfork parent handler — which on
one machine (0.1.1981) found its own lock unlocked and aborted into a
spin that held the gateway unresponsive for 57 minutes. Where reads
fail — no proxy set, scutil gone — noneKeep forked scutil every 2
seconds while requests flowed, each a fresh roll of those dice.

The reads after failed ones are now put off twice the none window
after the first failure, twice that after the next, and so on up to a
minute (failKeep); one that answers resets the run. A set proxy is
kept for its 15 seconds as before, and a read that answers within
readWait is still what the request waiting for it goes through (#3421).

The tool's read window (toolWait) is exported as ToolWait, so a test
can shorten it without reaching into the package's own name space.

Tests: TestFailedSystemProxyReadsBackOff (a failed read keeps the
proxy read before, the reads after it back off up to failKeep, an
answering one resets that), TestRequestsKeepGoingWhileReadsFail (a
request whose system read never answers is answered from the cache
without waiting readWait).

Fixes #4169
Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
